{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T18:47:25.223Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "mail/addr-spec takes the FIRST angle-bracket group in a From header, and the display-name phrase is fully sender-controlled, so From: \"<seb@corp.com>\" <mallory@evil.com> parses to seb@corp.com - the exact harvest the docstring says it NEVER does. That value is the key into :from->actor, so ingest mints ticket/create, artifact/attach and every tik> fact under the victim's actor name. Confirmed end to end against a file store. Guards read the actor through fact-status :by, so signed-by role gates are satisfied by the spoofed name; verify L1 catches it afterwards ONLY when the bridge signs (unsigned bridges get the unsigned note, not a failure). require-dkim! blocks it because from-domain comes from the same spoofed address and fails alignment - but :dkim :require is off by default, which is the documented MTA-agnostic procmail mode. Parse the addr-spec with quoted-string awareness (take the LAST bracket group, or strip quoted phrases first), reject a From carrying more than one address, and consider defaulting the DKIM gate on."} :event/parents #{"sha256-53227890da9ecffccdc89f02ef6bf57b0cffea7b7bd532aa30cf8dce41c789ac"} :event/ticket #uuid "fa3f6b49-251e-4f10-abb4-152eac741cf9" :event/type :fact/assert}